content.text:
The ProductGallery component now renders a 300×200 image for each product, and the TypeScript check passes.

In `app/ProductGallery.tsx` I followed the pattern already used for the hero image in `app/page.tsx`: import `Image` from `next/image` and render it with explicit dimensions. Each product now gets:

```tsx
<Image
  src={product.imageUrl}
  alt={product.name}
  width={300}
  height={200}
/>
```

I used the product name as the `alt` text so each image has a meaningful description, and removed the TODO comments since they're now resolved. I left out `priority`, since that's only appropriate for the single above-the-fold hero image, not a list of gallery items.

One thing to be aware of: the image files (`/product-1.jpg`, etc.) and `/hero-image.jpg` don't exist in the repo yet (there's no `public/` directory), so the images will 404 at runtime until those assets are added.
